  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 5's missing return route was solved. The second gravity switch must be clicked from the center safe column before entering either pillar-aligned trap-door column. After reversing upward, the two open-X toggle blocks below hanging pillars must first be solidified; they become a protective ceiling that permits the left-shaft ascent. The final 3x2 E barrier is a horizontal tunnel: enter from its lower-right cell, remove only the lower row from right to left, and leave the upper row intact as a shield against three hanging pillar eyes. Level 6 provisionally reuses the shield mechanic: solidifying its two lower X blocks before the first gravity flip creates a safe landing shelf, while stepping left off that shelf is lethal.",
  "narrative": "Resolved and replayed the 121-action verified prefix and confirmed frame.levels_completed == 4 before exploration. Two failed L5 routes established the safe switch timing and the role of the X shields; a third fresh-prefix attempt followed the 43-action extension recorded here and personally observed frame.levels_completed advance from 4 to 5. Only 114 calls remained at that live win, fewer than the 164 required to run reproduce() on the full candidate, so reproduction_verified is conservatively false. I spent seven further actions mapping L6: its first switch is survivable after solidifying the two lower X blocks, but stepping left from the resulting shelf killed the player. With 107 calls left, restoring the 121-action prefix was impossible, so exploration stopped.",
  "gotchas": [
    "env.reset() returns to the start of the whole game, not the start of level 5; each new exploration life costs the full 121-action prefix.",
    "ACTION7 is a no-op during normal play and does not restart the level after GAME_OVER; after GAME_OVER it returned an empty level-0 frame.",
    "A same-environment reset-and-prefix replay diverged once and ended at level 0, while genuinely fresh environments replayed the prefix correctly; use a fresh env/scorecard for reliable restoration.",
    "The second gravity switch is visible before the final trap-door columns. Flip it while the player is still in the center safe column; waiting until a door-aligned column is lethal.",
    "The E-door descent is not simply click-the-door-underfoot: opening a remote lower door and then taking a lateral move can trigger a long fall. Camera-relative click coordinates must be reread after every fall.",
    "Open-X toggle blocks are not merely passable gaps. Solidifying them creates shields that stop gravity before the player contacts a pillar eye; L5 requires solidifying both X blocks before traversing left under the pillars.",
    "At L5's final 3x2 E barrier, remove only the lower row from right to left. The untouched upper row is a ceiling shield; removing an upper cell exposes the player to its hanging pillar and creates a lethal pocket.",
    "L6 starts with open X blocks above downward pillars and below upward pillars. Solidifying the two lower X blocks before the first switch makes the initial fall safe, but the immediately adjacent left gap is lethal."
  ],
  "solve_provenance": "live_agent_self_discovery"
